  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New module `xtask/src/seed.rs`. Before its first step, `cargo xtask gate` copies the dependency units of another checkout into a new worktree. The units are `target/debug/{build,deps,.fingerprint}`. The source is the checkout of this repository with the most units.\n- The copy skips each package without a `source` in `cargo metadata`. These are the workspace members and the path dependencies.\n- The copy replaces a unit that is in the worktree already. `cargo xtask` builds its own dependencies before the gate starts, and their newer times made each copied unit above them dirty.\n- The copy keeps the file times. It copies outputs before fingerprints. It renames each unit into place.\n- The copy takes cargo's locks (`.cargo-lock`, `.cargo-build-lock`) without a wait. It passes over a checkout where a build runs.\n- A seeded worktree gets `target/debug/.camcraft-seeded` and is not seeded again. `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1` turns the seed off. A dry run does not seed.\n- `xtask/src/main.rs`: two module lines and one call in `gate`.\n- `docs/decisions/2575-seed-worktree-target.md`: the decision, the reasons and the dropped options.\n\n## Cause\n\nsccache 0.19 hashes three things that name the worktree in a Rust compile:\n- the `OUT_DIR` value of each env dependency;\n- the cwd;\n- the raw arguments.\n\nThus each crate with a build script misses in a new worktree, and each crate above it misses too (`solidcore`, `flecs`). `SCCACHE_BASEDIRS` applies only to C and C++ (`src/compiler/rust.rs`, hash key steps 3, 8 and 9). Cargo's own fingerprints do not name the worktree, so a copied unit reads as Fresh.\n\n## Readings (#914 comparison)\n\n18-core Mac, APFS, sccache 0.19 warm, `cargo xtask gate test after_defaults_to_none_and_writes_no_stream_word --crate app` in a new worktree:\n\n| | to the first app test | units compiled | `solidcore` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1` | 107 s (step 99 s) | 231 | compiled |\n| seeded | 42 s (seed 9 s, step 24 s) | 14 | Fresh |\n\nWith the seed, these compile: our 9 crates, plus `ring` and the 5 rustls crates above it. `ring` is dirty because \"the env variable CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR changed\" against the source checkout. I did not find why. The source checkout (`fix-2920`) was built by another session. Linux was not measured.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `xtask/src/seed_tests.rs`:\n- `a_seeded_checkout_finds_a_build_script_dependency_fresh`: two git dependencies, one with a build script that writes into `OUT_DIR`. Checkout `b` already has a newer unit of the lower dependency. After the seed, `cargo build -v` in `b` shows `Fresh seeddep`, and the local package compiles.\n- `a_checkout_where_a_build_runs_is_passed_over`\n- `local_packages_are_the_ones_without_a_source`\n- `a_unit_entry_of_a_local_package_is_never_copied`\n\nRed before the fix (no-op seed): `fresh-worktree build-script dependency must not compile again: Compiling seeddep v0.1.0 ...`.\n\nMutations:\n- Copy local packages too: red (`the local package compiles in b`). The stale unit read as Fresh.\n- Skip units that exist (no replace): red (`Dirty seeddep ...: the dependency seedbase was rebuilt`).\n- Do not keep the file times: green on APFS. `clonefile` keeps the times on macOS. The guard is for Linux and Windows copies, and it is not pinned on this machine.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (xtask unit tests). `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Linux and Windows. `fs::copy` uses `copy_file_range` on Linux (a reflink on btrfs and XFS, a full copy on ext4). On Windows it uses `CopyFileExW`.\n- Disk use on a file system without clones: the copy takes the size of the source's dependency units.\n- The gate skill does not describe the seed yet. The edit of `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md` needed an approval that this headless run did not have.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `xtask/src/main.rs` or the new files.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: The gate seeds a new worktree's `target/` from another checkout, so the dependencies (solidcore included) are not compiled again (`CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1` turns it off).\n\nFixes #2575\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
